CORE
main.json_symtab
_ --function main --program-only
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\(\d+\) r!0@1#\d+ == cprover_string_concat_func\("ab", "cd"\)$
^\(\d+\) r2!0@1#\d+ == cprover_string_substring_func\("ab", 0, 1\)$
^\(\d+\) r3!0@1#\d+ == cprover_string_replace_func\("ab", "a", "x"\)$
--
^Invariant check failed
_M_range_check
--
Value-returning (SMT-LIB-convention) applications of the string built-ins
have a String-typed result and no (length, content) output arguments. Symex's
string constant propagation must leave them alone rather than fail a
precondition of the refined-string convention. --program-only keeps this test
independent of the availability of an SMT solver.
